<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Nimoy returns three months after starting tiotropium-olodaterol and four days after finishing pulmonary rehabilitation. He attended all 24 sessions. He now walks about 300 meters at his own pace before stopping, uses the pursed-lip breathing he learned there, and has a home program of walking twice a day and strength exercises three times a week. He uses albuterol about twice a week, mostly before longer walks. He has taken every maintenance dose. He has had no flare-up, antibiotic or prednisone course, or emergency visit. He repeated the 6-minute walk in the pulmonary function laboratory this morning. The pneumococcal vaccine that was out of stock at the last visit is available today. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rehabilitation</td><td>Completed 24 of 24 sessions four days ago; home program in place</td></tr><tr><td>Exercise tolerance</td><td>Walks about 300 meters before stopping</td></tr><tr><td>Reliever use</td><td>Albuterol about twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>All maintenance doses taken</td></tr><tr><td>Exacerbations</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

