    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">COPD, GOLD 3, group B, improved after rehabilitation (J44.9)</content>. CAT 15, down from 22 at intake; mMRC grade 2, down from 3. 6-minute walk 330 m, 60 m farther than at rehabilitation entry, with a lowest saturation of 90 percent. Resting saturation 94 percent. Still group B, with no exacerbations. [S]<list><item>Continue tiotropium-olodaterol and albuterol as needed.</item><item>Keep up the home exercise program; a maintenance exercise class was offered.</item><item>PCV20 given today.</item><item>Spirometry again at the yearly review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>COPD Assessment Test (CAT)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>15, down from 19 at four weeks and 22 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>mMRC dyspnea grade</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Grade 2, down from 3</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Exacerbation history and GOLD group</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None; group B</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Pulse oximetry</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>94 percent at rest on room air</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Smoking status and cessation support</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Former smoker; no tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>BMI and nutritional status</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>BMI 23.6; weight up 0.6 kg with exercise</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Inhaler technique and adherence</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Correct; full adherence</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>6-minute walk test</td><td>At pulmonary rehabilitation entry and exit, and for oxygen assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>330 m at rehabilitation exit, up 60 m; lowest saturation 90 percent</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Long-term oxygen assessment</td><td>As indicated: resting saturation 88 percent or less, confirmed twice at least three weeks apart</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Resting saturation 94 percent; no oxygen criterion met</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Pulmonary rehabilitation</td><td>Stable mMRC 2 or more or CAT 10 or more; within three weeks of any hospital stay for an exacerbation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Program completed four days ago, 24 of 24 sessions; home program and maintenance class offered</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Spirometry</td><td>At diagnosis, then at least yearly and with significant clinical change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Next in nine months, at the yearly review</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Blood eosinophil count</td><td>At baseline and when an inhaled corticosteroid is considered</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No change in inhaled corticosteroid being considered</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Vaccination status</td><td>Reviewed yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today, nine weeks later than planned. Deviation: the dose planned at the four-week visit was missed because the vaccine was out of stock. No harm resulted: he had no respiratory infection in the interval. Corrective action: vaccine stock is checked before a planned dose is booked, and missed doses are added to the next visit&apos;s orders</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>CAT score at least 2 points lower by the three-month review. Outcome by 2026-05-12: CAT fell from 22 to 15 [S]</item><item>6-minute walk distance at least 30 meters farther after pulmonary rehabilitation. Outcome by 2026-05-12: 270 m at entry and 330 m at exit [S]</item><item>No moderate or severe exacerbation over the six months after starting maintenance therapy. In progress; target 2026-08-11 [S]</item><item>Correct soft mist inhaler technique and a daily maintenance dose. Outcome by 2026-03-10: Correct technique on demonstration and no missed doses by dose counter at four weeks [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for the Diagnosis, Management, and Prevention of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, 2025 report (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease monograph (2026); Pulmonary Rehabilitation for Adults with Chronic Respiratory Disease: An Official American Thoracic Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2023); Home Oxygen Therapy for Adults with Chronic Lung Disease: An Official American Thoracic Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2020); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: COPD review in three months, or the same day for any flare-up. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-11: six-month COPD review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
